  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">humanitarian crisis response in front-line and de-occupied communities of the Kherson region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">within the framework of the project Save the World expects to be able to help 500 households and prepare about 1,200 beneficiaries for winter. StW planS to deliver 2.0 tons of fuel briquettes for 500 households in the Kherson region. The total amount of fuel briquettes that we intend to deliver to the victims is 1,000 tons.Based on the developed questionnaire profile, the social worker will conduct a survey of beneficiaries according to the lists provided by the community. At the same time, he/she will be involved, if possible, in the process of on-site monitoring missions, formation of personal files of beneficiaries.If, during the implementation of the project, based on the results of the questionnaire, the team discovers other unique needs of the beneficiaries, for example, a request for free legal assistance, then the applicants will be referred to a lawyer of our foundation. This type of assistance is an own contribution.</narrative>
  </description>
